            <ArticleTitle>[The nurse and postoperating pain: the perception of pain phenomenon].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to the existing guidelines, nurses &quot;...collaborate in identifying the health needs of the person and the nursing requirements, plan, put into practice and evaluate the caring procedures...ensure that diagnostic and therapeutic procedures are correctly performed...&quot; Legislation governing professional responsibility obliges nurses to &quot;care for the sick person and to take action to alleviate symptoms, especially those that can be prevented&quot;. In daily clinical practice, the evaluation and treatment of pain does not always coincide with the recommendations, from both a legislative and ethical point of view.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
